In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Job Description:
We are seeking an experienced and reliable Window Fitter to join our team in Galway. The successful candidate will be responsible for fitting, repairing and replacing glass installations in residential and commercial properties while ensuring high standards of workmanship and safety.

Key Duties and Responsibilities:
Examines drawings and specifications to determine job requirements and measurements;
Measures, cuts and prepares plain, coloured, safety and ornamental glass for installation;
Smoothes and finishes glass edges and positions glass securely into frames or grooved lead strips;
Applies mastic, putty or adhesive between glass and frames and removes excess material for a clean finish;
Installs mirror panels on interior and exterior walls;
Repairs and replaces damaged or broken glass panels and fittings;
Ensures all fitting and glazing work is completed in accordance with safety standards and company procedures.

Requirements:
Previous experience as a Window Fitter, Glazier or similar role;
Ability to read technical drawings and specifications;
Good manual dexterity and attention to detail;
Knowledge of glass fitting materials, tools and installation techniques;
Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
Good communication skills and strong work ethic.

Employment Type: Full-time, Permanent
Salary: Competitive salary depending on experience.

In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Nicolas Krause, based in Dublin 15, Ireland, is seeking an experienced Window Fitter to join the business on a permanent, full-time basis. The successful candidate will carry out window and glazing installation, repair and replacement works at residential and commercial sites in Dublin and other locations where the business operates.

Main duties and responsibilities include: 
- Examining drawings, measurements and specifications to determine job requirements; 
- Removing existing windows, doors and damaged glazing and preparing openings for installation; 
- Installing, fitting and securing window and door units; 
- Measuring, cutting and positioning glass where required; 
- Applying sealants, mastic, putty or adhesives and ensuring proper alignment and weatherproofing; 
- Repairing or replacing damaged glass, windows and related components; 
- Ensuring all work is completed safely and to the required quality standards.

The successful candidate must have at least 1 year of relevant experience in window fitting, glazing or a similar role and must be capable of carrying out installation and repair work independently and to a high standard.

Employment type: Permanent, Full-Time
Working hours: 39 hours per week
Salary: €38.000 gross per annum
Location: Dublin 15, Ireland, with work carried out at various residential and commercial sites where the business operates.

To apply, please send your CV to contact.nicolaskrause@gmail.com

